WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:14.810
Zann's friends headed toward the wormhole.

2
00:00:15.691 --> 00:00:18.592
Zann noticed that Gliss' arms and legs were shaking.

3
00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:23.995
He winced, remembering how painful it had looked when she'd ripped off the magical goggles.

4
00:00:24.015 --> 00:00:26.497
"Wait," he said to his friends.

5
00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:28.658
"Are you sure you want to come with me?

6
00:00:29.158 --> 00:00:30.799
I mean, really sure?

7
00:00:31.639 --> 00:00:32.680
It could be dangerous.

8
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.921
Especially if Morb is involved."

9
00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:38.063
"Of course we're sure," Perda said.

10
00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:39.144
"Right, guys?"

11
00:00:40.344 --> 00:00:42.666
Gliss was still trembling, but she smiled.

12
00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:45.607
"You'd better not quit now, Zann.

13
00:00:46.048 --> 00:00:49.290
I don't want to think I defied Wyssa's command for nothing!"

14
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:52.171
"Yeah." Darb took Gliss' hand.

15
00:00:52.191 --> 00:00:54.473
"Besides, we make a good team.

16
00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:55.673
And we want to help."

17
00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:57.895
"Okay. Thanks."

18
00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:00.096
Zann glanced at the wormhole.

19
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:03.346
"But we don't have Wyssa to guide us anymore.

20
00:01:03.766 --> 00:01:04.687
We need a plan."

21
00:01:04.707 --> 00:01:06.588
"Good point."

22
00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:09.550
Perda paced back and forth in front of the wormhole.

23
00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.052
"Does anyone have any good ideas?"

24
00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:17.116
"Wyssa said Morb left a bunch of terrified worlds behind him," Darb said.

25
00:01:17.136 --> 00:01:21.319
"Maybe we could start visiting worlds and asking people about Morb.

26
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:23.060
That might give us some clues."

27
00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:25.222
Zann shook his head.

28
00:01:25.242 --> 00:01:28.224
"I'm not sure we should visit worlds randomly.

29
00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:31.891
We might end up back in that no-magic world again."

30
00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:33.992
Perda shuddered.

31
00:01:34.413 --> 00:01:38.696
"Or Fardark, or stinky Niffia, or that crazy cloud world."

32
00:01:39.637 --> 00:01:40.618
She was still pacing.

33
00:01:40.998 --> 00:01:44.541
Just then her foot hit a stone, which tumbled toward Zann.

34
00:01:44.561 --> 00:01:49.345
"Hey, check it out," said Zann, bending down to pick up the stone.

35
00:01:49.365 --> 00:01:52.708
"This looks just like my message stone!"

36
00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:54.650
Perda shrugged.

37
00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:55.550
"So what?

38
00:01:56.051 --> 00:01:57.132
It looks like a stone."

39
00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:01.867
"No, I mean I think they're the same type of stone."

40
00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.690
Zann fished out his message stone.

41
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.071
It still felt warm.

42
00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:09.214
He held the two stones side by side.

43
00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:12.257
"See?" "Weird," Darb said.

44
00:02:12.277 --> 00:02:13.798
"They do look alike."

45
00:02:14.679 --> 00:02:15.780
Gliss glanced around.

46
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.803
"Look, there are more stones like that!"

47
00:02:19.984 --> 00:02:20.545
She was right.

48
00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:23.748
Dozens of similar stones lay near the wormhole.

49
00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:30.147
"I assumed my stone came from the Cave of the Unknown because I'd never seen one like it

50
00:02:30.387 --> 00:02:32.568
anywhere else in Magica," said Zann.

51
00:02:32.588 --> 00:02:36.130
"But maybe it actually came from this world."

52
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.932
"That makes sense," Darb said.

53
00:02:38.952 --> 00:02:40.993
"This is Wyssa's home world, right?

54
00:02:41.773 --> 00:02:45.215
That's probably why she used that stone to communicate with your parents."

55
00:02:46.656 --> 00:02:48.337
"And with Morb," Perda added.

56
00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:53.320
"It also explains why none of us had ever heard of message stones before."

57
00:02:54.344 --> 00:02:57.287
"Teplo and Boz knew about them," Gliss pointed out.

58
00:02:58.047 --> 00:02:58.768
Perda shrugged.

59
00:02:59.108 --> 00:03:00.389
"They're Magic Masters.

60
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.792
It's their job to know lots of obscure stuff."

61
00:03:05.053 --> 00:03:06.915
Zann squeezed the stone in his hand.

62
00:03:07.816 --> 00:03:14.061
If his stone came from this world, that might explain why he'd had that extra-vivid dream here earlier.

63
00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:18.985
"I think we should look for a place to play my parents' message again," he said.

64
00:03:19.005 --> 00:03:20.986
"There might be more clues."

65
00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:24.128
"Clues? Like what?"

66
00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:25.709
Perda sounded dubious.

67
00:03:25.729 --> 00:03:31.031
"I don't see any place to plug in the stone," said Gliss, looking around.

68
00:03:31.051 --> 00:03:33.632
"She’s right,” Perda said.

69
00:03:33.652 --> 00:03:36.293
"Anyway, I just thought of another plan.

70
00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:38.454
We should try to follow Wyssa.

71
00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:41.375
She's looking for Morb, right?

72
00:03:41.836 --> 00:03:43.776
And Morb is looking for Zann's parents.

73
00:03:44.577 --> 00:03:48.739
So if we can catch up to Wyssa, we might find Zann's parents too."

74
00:03:48.759 --> 00:03:52.040
"Wyssa left a while ago, though," Darb said.

75
00:03:52.844 --> 00:03:54.945
"We'll never find her in the vortex now."

76
00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:58.346
"Besides, how do we know we can trust her?"

77
00:03:58.626 --> 00:03:59.206
Zann asked.

78
00:03:59.226 --> 00:04:03.027
"Wyssa was the one who brought those flizzes to Morb.

79
00:04:03.607 --> 00:04:06.008
She also tried to bring him a scatter beast."

80
00:04:07.128 --> 00:04:08.888
"That was earlier," Perda said.

81
00:04:08.908 --> 00:04:11.149
"She's not working with Morb anymore."

82
00:04:12.049 --> 00:04:12.789
Darb shrugged.

83
00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.170
"Still, she may not be on our side.

84
00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:20.391
She broke Zann's Shackle spell and put that nasty spell on Gliss, remember?"

85
00:04:21.312 --> 00:04:21.972
Gliss nodded.

86
00:04:22.436 --> 00:04:27.560
"Plus, she used a Truth spell on Zann without his consent, and—oh!

87
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.520
That's it!"

88
00:04:29.361 --> 00:04:30.021
"That's what?"

89
00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:30.882
Perda asked.

90
00:04:32.003 --> 00:04:33.664
Gliss pointed at Zann's forehead.

91
00:04:33.684 --> 00:04:41.329
"Look! When Wyssa touched Zann's face to do the Truth spell, she left purple fingerprints on his skin!"

92
00:04:41.349 --> 00:04:42.970
"She did?"

93
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.752
Zann said, reaching up to wipe away the marks.

94
00:04:45.772 --> 00:04:51.676
"Stop!" Perda leaped forward, grabbing Zann's hands before he could touch his forehead.

95
00:04:52.608 --> 00:04:53.849
"Don't wipe them off.

96
00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.153
Maybe we can use that purple stuff to track Wyssa the same way she used it to track

97
00:04:59.193 --> 00:05:00.134
Gliss and Darb!"

98
00:05:00.154 --> 00:05:04.898
"I was thinking the same thing," said Gliss with a smile.

99
00:05:05.739 --> 00:05:10.883
"You mean we can figure out which wormholes have been used recently, and see if she's in those

100
00:05:10.963 --> 00:05:12.264
worlds?" Zann said.

101
00:05:13.105 --> 00:05:14.165
Perda looked excited.

102
00:05:14.185 --> 00:05:16.367
"It's the only good plan we have.

103
00:05:17.008 --> 00:05:18.189
What do you say, Zann?"

104
00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.172
Zann turned his message stone over in his hand.

105
00:05:22.944 --> 00:05:24.005
"You're right," he said.

106
00:05:24.025 --> 00:05:25.987
"Let's not waste any more time."

107
00:05:26.007 --> 00:05:29.230
"Okay." Gliss glanced at the wormhole.

108
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:33.273
"We'd better make sure we're all shackled together this time.

109
00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:36.176
We don't want to get separated again."

110
00:05:36.196 --> 00:05:37.937
"Good idea."

111
00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.338
Perda held out her hands.

112
00:05:39.358 --> 00:05:41.180
"Join friction, everyone.

113
00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.964
We'll make this one a Mutual Shackle spell so any of us can break it if we need

114
00:05:46.024 --> 00:05:50.428
to." "Just don't do that in the vortex," Zann warned.

115
00:05:51.344 --> 00:05:53.426
Soon the four of them were shackled together.

116
00:05:54.307 --> 00:05:56.588
Zann even conjured a harness for Zing.

117
00:05:56.609 --> 00:05:58.270
"Everyone ready?"

118
00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.071
Darb asked.

119
00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.552
"Let's go!"

120
00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:03.094
Perda said, leading the way toward the wormhole.

121
00:06:03.955 --> 00:06:07.177
Zann held his breath as they all dived into the vortex.

122
00:06:08.598 --> 00:06:11.160
It felt much scarier being there without Wyssa.

123
00:06:11.581 --> 00:06:13.022
But he tried not to think about that.

124
00:06:13.042 --> 00:06:15.044
"It's working!"

125
00:06:15.264 --> 00:06:17.486
Gliss cried, staring at Zann's forehead.

126
00:06:17.506 --> 00:06:20.068
"The fingerprints are glowing!"

127
00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.602
Zann's left hand was shackled to Perda.

128
00:06:24.503 --> 00:06:27.165
He used his right hand to grab the nearest wormhole.

129
00:06:28.286 --> 00:06:29.347
"Hang on, everyone!"

130
00:06:29.587 --> 00:06:31.689
he cried as he yanked his friends through.

131
00:06:32.609 --> 00:06:35.732
He felt the familiar sensation of passing through the wormhole.

132
00:06:36.212 --> 00:06:38.434
It felt weird but not unpleasant.

133
00:06:40.796 --> 00:06:42.317
Splash! "Drat!

134
00:06:43.378 --> 00:06:45.360
Aah!" Zann screamed in horror.

135
00:06:46.161 --> 00:06:49.083
They had just landed in a pool of boiling water!
